The meanings of “solemn” and “stern” may be a result of phonetic borrowing.

===Etymology===
{{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} considers {{och-l|嚴}} to be cognate with the following:
* {{och-l|巖|''(of mountains)'' high; lofty}}
* {{och-l|儼|dignified; majestic}}
* {{och-l|險|precipitous; dangerous}}
* {{och-l|業|lofty; large}} (an allofam with a stop final).

They are all [[Sino-Tibetan]] in origin. Cognates in Tibetan include {{cog|bo|རྔམ་པ་||splendor; majesty}} and {{cog|bo|རྔམས||height; splendor}}. {{cog|my|ငြမ်း||scaffold}} may also be a cognate.

