===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|よ}}
{{IPAfont|⟨yo<sub>2</sub>⟩}} → *{{IPAfont|/jə/}} → {{IPAfont|/jo/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*yə}}.

In modern Japanese, Japonic {{ja-r|よ}} is more common than Sinitic {{ja-r|し|pos=see Etymology 3}} outside fixed compounds, which is similar to {{ja-r|七|なな}} but different from other numerals. The reason may be a superstitious connection to {{ja-r|死|し|death}}, or simply avoiding confusion with similar sounding {{ja-r|一|いち|one}} and {{ja-r|七|しち|seven}}.

